    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10), our two highest-rated starters. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an aggressive boost due to the favorable matchup against Arrighetti (4.66 xERA) and the efficiency of the #2 spot in the order, while **Jackson Merrill** thrives in a prime opportunity against Dobnak. Complementing this, our middle-infield stack of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) are prioritized due to high-ceiling matchups against J.T. Ginn and Zack Littell respectively, both of whom carry elevated xERA marks that suggest significant scoring potential. **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) also represents a high-value play; the combination of a +14% park factor and the premium #3 lineup spot makes him a vital contributor to our speed-focused strategy.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the board was the exclusion of **Nasim Nunez** (61.09) from the active lineup. While **Nasim Nunez** brings the elite sprint speed necessary for our 5x5 objectives, his projected #9 spot in the batting order created a drag on his overall efficiency score, ultimately keeping him on the bench in favor of higher-order hitters like **Drake Baldwin** (58.73) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.14). We are closely monitoring the status of **Kyle Tucker** (55.51) and **Andy Pages** (52.49); both are currently facing a lower-floor scenario against the left-handed Ryan Weathers. Their scores reflect the inherent risk of the platoon disadvantage, and we will be scanning for late-breaking lineup changes to ensure we aren't exposed to excessive defensive substitution risk if a high-leverage pinch hitter is signaled.",
